{"key":"nlp-basics-u2-02","seriesId":"nlp-basics","episode":"u2-02","title":"Part-of-Speech Tagging: Is It a Noun or a Verb?","fps":30,"duration":224.121,"durationInFrames":6724,"video":{"width":1920,"height":1080,"burnCaptions":true,"brand":"learnvi.in"},"badge":["UNIT 2 · LESSON 2","POS TAGGING"],"series":{"title":"NLP, Simply Explained","subtitle":"University NLP, one idea at a time, no heavy maths","runningPrompt":"","stops":[{"id":"u1-01","number":1,"name":"The Stages of NLP: From Letters to Meaning","stamp":"THE STAGES OF NLP: FROM LETTERS TO MEANING","topic":""},{"id":"u1-02","number":2,"name":"Tokenization: How Text Becomes Pieces","stamp":"TOKENIZATION: HOW TEXT BECOMES PIECES","topic":""},{"id":"u1-03","number":3,"name":"Text Classification: Teaching Computers to Sort Text","stamp":"TEXT CLASSIFICATION: TEACHING COMPUTERS TO SORT TEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u2-01","number":4,"name":"Morphology: The Building Blocks Inside Words","stamp":"MORPHOLOGY: THE BUILDING BLOCKS INSIDE WORDS","topic":""},{"id":"u2-02","number":5,"name":"Part-of-Speech Tagging: Is It a Noun or a Verb?","stamp":"PART-OF-SPEECH TAGGING: IS IT A NOUN OR A VERB?","topic":""},{"id":"u4-01","number":6,"name":"Word Vectors: Giving Words a Place on a Map","stamp":"WORD VECTORS: GIVING WORDS A PLACE ON A MAP","topic":""}]},"stop":{"number":5,"name":"Part-of-Speech Tagging: Is It a Noun or a Verb?","stamp":"PART-OF-SPEECH TAGGING: IS IT A NOUN OR A VERB?"},"shorts":{"width":1080,"height":1920,"maxSeconds":60,"cta":"Full lesson: NLP, Simply Explained · Unit 2"},"thumbnail":{"headline":"Noun or verb? How AI decides","big":"book · book"},"segments":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","component":"TitleCard","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c01","start":0.6,"end":6.935,"marks":{},"text":"Welcome back to NLP, Simply Explained. This is unit 2, lesson 2: part-of-speech tagging.","words":[{"w":"Welcome","start":0.6},{"w":"back","start":1.08},{"w":"to","start":1.427},{"w":"NLP,","start":1.773},{"w":"Simply","start":2.12},{"w":"Explained.","start":2.76},{"w":"This","start":3.52},{"w":"is","start":3.8},{"w":"unit","start":4.04},{"w":"2,","start":4.413},{"w":"lesson","start":4.787},{"w":"2:","start":5.16},{"w":"part-of-speech","start":5.8},{"w":"tagging.","start":6.44}]},{"id":"c02","start":7.335,"end":12.737,"marks":{},"text":"Last time we looked inside words. Today we look at the job each word does in a sentence.","words":[{"w":"Last","start":7.335},{"w":"time","start":7.695},{"w":"we","start":7.975},{"w":"looked","start":8.175},{"w":"inside","start":8.415},{"w":"words.","start":9.015},{"w":"Today","start":9.495},{"w":"we","start":9.975},{"w":"look","start":10.175},{"w":"at","start":10.375},{"w":"the","start":10.495},{"w":"job","start":10.615},{"w":"each","start":11.055},{"w":"word","start":11.335},{"w":"does","start":11.575},{"w":"in","start":11.895},{"w":"a","start":12.015},{"w":"sentence.","start":12.135}]}],"title":"Welcome","shortTitle":"Welcome","props":{"kicker":"Unit 2 · Lesson 2","title":"Part-of-Speech Tagging","subtitle":"Is it a noun or a verb?"},"start":0.6,"end":12.737,"startFrame":0,"durationInFrames":410},{"id":"idea","kind":"core","component":"BigIdea","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c03","start":13.667,"end":22.176,"marks":{},"text":"Here is the idea for today. The same word can play different roles in different sentences. Part-of-speech tagging works out which role it's playing.","words":[{"w":"Here","start":13.667},{"w":"is","start":13.987},{"w":"the","start":14.147},{"w":"idea","start":14.307},{"w":"for","start":14.787},{"w":"today.","start":15.187},{"w":"The","start":15.587},{"w":"same","start":15.827},{"w":"word","start":16.147},{"w":"can","start":16.467},{"w":"play","start":16.627},{"w":"different","start":16.907},{"w":"roles","start":17.307},{"w":"in","start":17.667},{"w":"different","start":17.827},{"w":"sentences.","start":18.227},{"w":"Part-of-speech","start":19.167},{"w":"tagging","start":20.107},{"w":"works","start":20.547},{"w":"out","start":20.867},{"w":"which","start":21.027},{"w":"role","start":21.267},{"w":"it's","start":21.507},{"w":"playing.","start":21.747}]}],"title":"The big idea","shortTitle":"The big idea","props":{"kicker":"Key idea","text":"The same word can play different roles. Tagging works out which one.","highlight":["different roles"]},"start":13.667,"end":22.176,"startFrame":410,"durationInFrames":283},{"id":"pos","kind":"core","component":"Definition","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c04","start":23.1,"end":29.796,"marks":{},"text":"A part of speech is the grammatical role a word plays in a sentence: noun, verb, adjective, and so on.","words":[{"w":"A","start":23.1},{"w":"part","start":23.22},{"w":"of","start":23.42},{"w":"speech","start":23.54},{"w":"is","start":23.9},{"w":"the","start":24.02},{"w":"grammatical","start":24.14},{"w":"role","start":24.82},{"w":"a","start":25.1},{"w":"word","start":25.26},{"w":"plays","start":25.5},{"w":"in","start":25.82},{"w":"a","start":25.94},{"w":"sentence:","start":26.06},{"w":"noun,","start":26.793},{"w":"verb,","start":27.527},{"w":"adjective,","start":28.26},{"w":"and","start":29.02},{"w":"so","start":29.22},{"w":"on.","start":29.46}]},{"id":"c05","start":30.196,"end":33.734,"marks":{},"text":"In \"book a flight\", the word \"book\" is a verb. It's something you do.","words":[{"w":"In","start":30.196},{"w":"\"book","start":30.316},{"w":"a","start":30.516},{"w":"flight\",","start":30.716},{"w":"the","start":31.036},{"w":"word","start":31.236},{"w":"\"book\"","start":31.476},{"w":"is","start":31.796},{"w":"a","start":32.036},{"w":"verb.","start":32.276},{"w":"It's","start":32.516},{"w":"something","start":32.836},{"w":"you","start":33.156},{"w":"do.","start":33.436}]},{"id":"c06","start":34.134,"end":42.659,"marks":{},"text":"Think of words as actors. The same actor can play the hero in one film and the villain in the next. You can only tell which by watching the scene.","words":[{"w":"Think","start":34.134},{"w":"of","start":34.374},{"w":"words","start":34.534},{"w":"as","start":34.934},{"w":"actors.","start":35.174},{"w":"The","start":35.894},{"w":"same","start":36.134},{"w":"actor","start":36.494},{"w":"can","start":36.934},{"w":"play","start":37.094},{"w":"the","start":37.334},{"w":"hero","start":37.494},{"w":"in","start":37.894},{"w":"one","start":38.094},{"w":"film","start":38.294},{"w":"and","start":38.694},{"w":"the","start":38.854},{"w":"villain","start":39.014},{"w":"in","start":39.414},{"w":"the","start":39.574},{"w":"next.","start":39.734},{"w":"You","start":40.214},{"w":"can","start":40.454},{"w":"only","start":40.694},{"w":"tell","start":40.934},{"w":"which","start":41.214},{"w":"by","start":41.454},{"w":"watching","start":41.654},{"w":"the","start":42.094},{"w":"scene.","start":42.254}]}],"title":"What is a part of speech?","shortTitle":"What is a part of speech?","props":{"kicker":"Definition","term":"Part of speech","definition":"The grammatical role a word plays in a sentence: noun, verb, adjective, and so on.","example":"book a flight → book = verb","analogy":"Roles in a play: one actor can be the hero or the villain."},"start":23.1,"end":42.659,"startFrame":693,"durationInFrames":614},{"id":"tagset","kind":"core","component":"Table","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c07","start":43.567,"end":48.511,"marks":{},"text":"A tagger gives every word a short label called a tag. Here are six you'll see everywhere.","words":[{"w":"A","start":43.567},{"w":"tagger","start":43.867},{"w":"gives","start":44.167},{"w":"every","start":44.487},{"w":"word","start":44.727},{"w":"a","start":44.967},{"w":"short","start":45.127},{"w":"label","start":45.407},{"w":"called","start":45.847},{"w":"a","start":46.127},{"w":"tag.","start":46.247},{"w":"Here","start":46.687},{"w":"are","start":47.007},{"w":"six","start":47.207},{"w":"you'll","start":47.447},{"w":"see","start":47.727},{"w":"everywhere.","start":47.967}]},{"id":"c08","start":48.911,"end":52.088,"marks":{},"text":"NOUN is a thing or an idea, like \"cat\" or \"flight\".","words":[{"w":"NOUN","start":48.911},{"w":"is","start":49.231},{"w":"a","start":49.391},{"w":"thing","start":49.551},{"w":"or","start":49.751},{"w":"an","start":49.911},{"w":"idea,","start":50.071},{"w":"like","start":50.591},{"w":"\"cat\"","start":50.911},{"w":"or","start":51.311},{"w":"\"flight\".","start":51.551}]},{"id":"c09","start":52.488,"end":56.792,"marks":{},"text":"VERB is an action or a state, like \"run\", or \"book\" when you book something.","words":[{"w":"VERB","start":52.528},{"w":"is","start":52.888},{"w":"an","start":53.008},{"w":"action","start":53.128},{"w":"or","start":53.568},{"w":"a","start":53.688},{"w":"state,","start":53.848},{"w":"like","start":54.248},{"w":"\"run\",","start":54.568},{"w":"or","start":55.008},{"w":"\"book\"","start":55.288},{"w":"when","start":55.648},{"w":"you","start":55.848},{"w":"book","start":56.008},{"w":"something.","start":56.328}]},{"id":"c10","start":57.192,"end":60.92,"marks":{},"text":"ADJ, short for adjective, describes a noun, like \"happy\" or \"red\".","words":[{"w":"ADJ,","start":57.352},{"w":"short","start":57.512},{"w":"for","start":57.752},{"w":"adjective,","start":57.912},{"w":"describes","start":58.512},{"w":"a","start":58.992},{"w":"noun,","start":59.112},{"w":"like","start":59.512},{"w":"\"happy\"","start":59.752},{"w":"or","start":60.232},{"w":"\"red\".","start":60.512}]},{"id":"c11","start":61.32,"end":64.932,"marks":{},"text":"DET, short for determiner, points to a noun, like \"the\" or \"a\".","words":[{"w":"DET,","start":61.48},{"w":"short","start":61.64},{"w":"for","start":61.88},{"w":"determiner,","start":62.04},{"w":"points","start":62.72},{"w":"to","start":63.04},{"w":"a","start":63.16},{"w":"noun,","start":63.24},{"w":"like","start":63.64},{"w":"\"the\"","start":63.96},{"w":"or","start":64.24},{"w":"\"a\".","start":64.56}]},{"id":"c12","start":65.332,"end":68.934,"marks":{},"text":"ADP covers prepositions, like \"in\", \"on\" and \"to\".","words":[{"w":"ADP","start":65.612},{"w":"covers","start":65.892},{"w":"prepositions,","start":66.292},{"w":"like","start":67.172},{"w":"\"in\",","start":67.452},{"w":"\"on\"","start":67.852},{"w":"and","start":68.212},{"w":"\"to\".","start":68.532}]},{"id":"c13","start":69.334,"end":73.951,"marks":{},"text":"And PRON is a pronoun, a word that stands in for a noun, like \"she\" or \"it\".","words":[{"w":"And","start":69.334},{"w":"PRON","start":69.574},{"w":"is","start":69.814},{"w":"a","start":69.974},{"w":"pronoun,","start":70.134},{"w":"a","start":70.694},{"w":"word","start":70.934},{"w":"that","start":71.174},{"w":"stands","start":71.374},{"w":"in","start":71.734},{"w":"for","start":71.894},{"w":"a","start":72.014},{"w":"noun,","start":72.174},{"w":"like","start":72.574},{"w":"\"she\"","start":72.894},{"w":"or","start":73.254},{"w":"\"it\".","start":73.614}]}],"title":"Common tags","shortTitle":"Common tags","props":{"kicker":"The tag set","title":"Six tags you'll see everywhere","columns":["Tag","Meaning","Examples"],"rows":[["NOUN","a thing or idea","cat · flight"],["VERB","an action or state","run · book"],["ADJ","describes a noun","happy · red"],["DET","points to a noun","the · a"],["ADP","preposition","in · on · to"],["PRON","stands in for a noun","she · it"]],"highlight":[]},"start":43.567,"end":73.951,"startFrame":1307,"durationInFrames":939},{"id":"tagged","kind":"core","component":"Table","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c14","start":74.867,"end":77.842,"marks":{},"text":"Let's tag a whole sentence: \"I want to book a flight\".","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":74.867},{"w":"tag","start":75.187},{"w":"a","start":75.427},{"w":"whole","start":75.587},{"w":"sentence:","start":75.827},{"w":"\"I","start":76.427},{"w":"want","start":76.707},{"w":"to","start":76.787},{"w":"book","start":76.867},{"w":"a","start":76.947},{"w":"flight\".","start":77.427}]},{"id":"c15","start":78.242,"end":79.412,"marks":{},"text":"\"I\" is a pronoun.","words":[{"w":"\"I\"","start":78.242},{"w":"is","start":78.442},{"w":"a","start":78.642},{"w":"pronoun.","start":78.762}]},{"id":"c16","start":79.812,"end":80.955,"marks":{},"text":"\"want\" is a verb.","words":[{"w":"\"want\"","start":79.812},{"w":"is","start":80.212},{"w":"a","start":80.46},{"w":"verb.","start":80.707}]},{"id":"c17","start":81.355,"end":85.917,"marks":{},"text":"\"to\" gets its own small tag, PART, because here it's part of the verb that follows.","words":[{"w":"\"to\"","start":81.395},{"w":"gets","start":81.555},{"w":"its","start":81.835},{"w":"own","start":82.115},{"w":"small","start":82.395},{"w":"tag,","start":82.675},{"w":"PART,","start":83.155},{"w":"because","start":83.515},{"w":"here","start":83.835},{"w":"it's","start":84.115},{"w":"part","start":84.395},{"w":"of","start":84.555},{"w":"the","start":84.755},{"w":"verb","start":84.955},{"w":"that","start":85.155},{"w":"follows.","start":85.355}]},{"id":"c18","start":86.317,"end":88.699,"marks":{},"text":"\"book\" is a verb: booking is the action.","words":[{"w":"\"book\"","start":86.317},{"w":"is","start":86.637},{"w":"a","start":86.877},{"w":"verb:","start":87.117},{"w":"booking","start":87.357},{"w":"is","start":87.797},{"w":"the","start":87.997},{"w":"action.","start":88.157}]},{"id":"c19","start":89.099,"end":90.386,"marks":{},"text":"\"a\" is a determiner.","words":[{"w":"\"a\"","start":89.099},{"w":"is","start":89.339},{"w":"a","start":89.499},{"w":"determiner.","start":89.659}]},{"id":"c20","start":90.786,"end":92.165,"marks":{},"text":"And \"flight\" is a noun.","words":[{"w":"And","start":90.786},{"w":"\"flight\"","start":90.946},{"w":"is","start":91.386},{"w":"a","start":91.586},{"w":"noun.","start":91.706}]}],"title":"A tagged sentence","shortTitle":"A tagged sentence","props":{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"“I want to book a flight”","columns":["Word","Tag"],"rows":[["I","PRON"],["want","VERB"],["to","PART"],["book","VERB"],["a","DET"],["flight","NOUN"]],"highlight":[{"row":3}]},"start":74.867,"end":92.165,"startFrame":2246,"durationInFrames":546},{"id":"book","kind":"core","component":"Compare","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c21","start":93.067,"end":96.275,"marks":{},"text":"Notice that \"book\" was a verb there. But it isn't always.","words":[{"w":"Notice","start":93.067},{"w":"that","start":93.547},{"w":"\"book\"","start":93.787},{"w":"was","start":94.067},{"w":"a","start":94.28},{"w":"verb","start":94.494},{"w":"there.","start":94.707},{"w":"But","start":94.947},{"w":"it","start":95.147},{"w":"isn't","start":95.347},{"w":"always.","start":95.707}]},{"id":"c22","start":96.675,"end":99.612,"marks":{},"text":"In \"book a flight\", it's a verb: an action you do.","words":[{"w":"In","start":96.675},{"w":"\"book","start":96.835},{"w":"a","start":96.995},{"w":"flight\",","start":97.155},{"w":"it's","start":97.555},{"w":"a","start":97.835},{"w":"verb:","start":98.115},{"w":"an","start":98.395},{"w":"action","start":98.595},{"w":"you","start":99.075},{"w":"do.","start":99.315}]},{"id":"c23","start":100.012,"end":103.378,"marks":{},"text":"In \"read a book\", it's a noun: a thing you hold in your hands.","words":[{"w":"In","start":100.092},{"w":"\"read","start":100.172},{"w":"a","start":100.452},{"w":"book\",","start":100.572},{"w":"it's","start":100.812},{"w":"a","start":101.092},{"w":"noun:","start":101.252},{"w":"a","start":101.652},{"w":"thing","start":101.852},{"w":"you","start":102.092},{"w":"hold","start":102.292},{"w":"in","start":102.612},{"w":"your","start":102.732},{"w":"hands.","start":102.972}]},{"id":"c24","start":103.778,"end":107.861,"marks":{},"text":"The spelling is identical, so the word alone can't tell you which it is.","words":[{"w":"The","start":103.778},{"w":"spelling","start":103.938},{"w":"is","start":104.418},{"w":"identical,","start":104.578},{"w":"so","start":105.378},{"w":"the","start":105.618},{"w":"word","start":105.818},{"w":"alone","start":106.018},{"w":"can't","start":106.498},{"w":"tell","start":106.818},{"w":"you","start":106.978},{"w":"which","start":107.218},{"w":"it","start":107.378},{"w":"is.","start":107.578}]},{"id":"c25","start":108.261,"end":112.103,"marks":{"verdict":110.381},"text":"What decides it is the company it keeps. The neighbouring words decide.","words":[{"w":"What","start":108.261},{"w":"decides","start":108.421},{"w":"it","start":108.941},{"w":"is","start":109.101},{"w":"the","start":109.261},{"w":"company","start":109.381},{"w":"it","start":109.781},{"w":"keeps.","start":109.941},{"w":"The","start":110.381},{"w":"neighbouring","start":110.501},{"w":"words","start":111.181},{"w":"decide.","start":111.541}]}],"title":"One word, two tags","shortTitle":"Why “book” confuses computers","props":{"kicker":"Ambiguity","title":"One word, two parts of speech","columns":[{"title":"Verb","items":["“book a flight”","an action you do"],"tone":"good","at":"c22"},{"title":"Noun","items":["“read a book”","a thing you hold"],"tone":"neutral","at":"c23"}],"verdict":{"text":"The neighbouring words decide","at":"c25@verdict"}},"start":93.067,"end":112.103,"startFrame":2792,"durationInFrames":599},{"id":"decide","kind":"core","component":"Steps","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c26","start":113.033,"end":116.654,"marks":{},"text":"So how does a tagger make the decision? It works in three steps.","words":[{"w":"So","start":113.033},{"w":"how","start":113.193},{"w":"does","start":113.353},{"w":"a","start":113.553},{"w":"tagger","start":113.813},{"w":"make","start":114.073},{"w":"the","start":114.273},{"w":"decision?","start":114.393},{"w":"It","start":115.033},{"w":"works","start":115.273},{"w":"in","start":115.633},{"w":"three","start":115.833},{"w":"steps.","start":116.113}]},{"id":"c27","start":117.054,"end":122.664,"marks":{},"text":"Look up: first it checks which tags each word is able to take. \"book\" could be a noun or a verb.","words":[{"w":"Look","start":117.054},{"w":"up:","start":117.294},{"w":"first","start":117.534},{"w":"it","start":117.734},{"w":"checks","start":117.934},{"w":"which","start":118.254},{"w":"tags","start":118.454},{"w":"each","start":118.814},{"w":"word","start":119.014},{"w":"is","start":119.214},{"w":"able","start":119.374},{"w":"to","start":119.654},{"w":"take.","start":119.854},{"w":"\"book\"","start":120.494},{"w":"could","start":120.974},{"w":"be","start":121.134},{"w":"a","start":121.294},{"w":"noun","start":121.454},{"w":"or","start":121.854},{"w":"a","start":122.124},{"w":"verb.","start":122.394}]},{"id":"c28","start":123.064,"end":127.386,"marks":{},"text":"Check neighbours: then it looks at what usually comes before and after each tag.","words":[{"w":"Check","start":123.064},{"w":"neighbours:","start":123.384},{"w":"then","start":124.024},{"w":"it","start":124.264},{"w":"looks","start":124.464},{"w":"at","start":124.704},{"w":"what","start":124.864},{"w":"usually","start":125.064},{"w":"comes","start":125.544},{"w":"before","start":125.904},{"w":"and","start":126.224},{"w":"after","start":126.424},{"w":"each","start":126.704},{"w":"tag.","start":126.944}]},{"id":"c29","start":127.786,"end":135.517,"marks":{},"text":"Pick the best: finally it chooses the tags that make the most sense for the whole sentence together, not just one word at a time.","words":[{"w":"Pick","start":127.786},{"w":"the","start":128.106},{"w":"best:","start":128.306},{"w":"finally","start":128.786},{"w":"it","start":129.466},{"w":"chooses","start":129.706},{"w":"the","start":130.186},{"w":"tags","start":130.346},{"w":"that","start":130.786},{"w":"make","start":130.986},{"w":"the","start":131.186},{"w":"most","start":131.306},{"w":"sense","start":131.546},{"w":"for","start":131.946},{"w":"the","start":132.066},{"w":"whole","start":132.226},{"w":"sentence","start":132.466},{"w":"together,","start":132.986},{"w":"not","start":133.626},{"w":"just","start":133.906},{"w":"one","start":134.186},{"w":"word","start":134.506},{"w":"at","start":134.826},{"w":"a","start":135.026},{"w":"time.","start":135.146}]}],"title":"How a tagger decides","shortTitle":"How a tagger decides","props":{"kicker":"Inside a tagger","title":"How a tagger decides","steps":[{"label":"Look up","detail":"which tags each word can take"},{"label":"Check neighbours","detail":"what usually comes before and after"},{"label":"Pick the best","detail":"the most likely tags for the whole sentence"}]},"start":113.033,"end":135.517,"startFrame":3391,"durationInFrames":702},{"id":"clues","kind":"core","component":"Bullets","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c30","start":136.433,"end":139.863,"marks":{},"text":"What kinds of clues does a tagger learn? Here are four simple ones.","words":[{"w":"What","start":136.433},{"w":"kinds","start":136.593},{"w":"of","start":136.833},{"w":"clues","start":136.953},{"w":"does","start":137.273},{"w":"a","start":137.473},{"w":"tagger","start":137.593},{"w":"learn?","start":137.913},{"w":"Here","start":138.273},{"w":"are","start":138.593},{"w":"four","start":138.753},{"w":"simple","start":138.993},{"w":"ones.","start":139.473}]},{"id":"c31","start":140.263,"end":143.419,"marks":{},"text":"After \"the\" or \"a\", the next word is usually a noun.","words":[{"w":"After","start":140.263},{"w":"\"the\"","start":140.663},{"w":"or","start":140.983},{"w":"\"a\",","start":141.223},{"w":"the","start":141.543},{"w":"next","start":141.743},{"w":"word","start":142.103},{"w":"is","start":142.343},{"w":"usually","start":142.503},{"w":"a","start":142.863},{"w":"noun.","start":143.023}]},{"id":"c32","start":143.819,"end":146.546,"marks":{},"text":"After \"to\", there's often a verb, as in \"to book\".","words":[{"w":"After","start":143.819},{"w":"\"to\",","start":144.139},{"w":"there's","start":144.459},{"w":"often","start":144.779},{"w":"a","start":145.046},{"w":"verb,","start":145.312},{"w":"as","start":145.579},{"w":"in","start":145.779},{"w":"\"to","start":145.939},{"w":"book\".","start":146.242}]},{"id":"c33","start":146.946,"end":150.619,"marks":{},"text":"A word ending in \"l y\" is often an adverb, like \"quickly\".","words":[{"w":"A","start":146.946},{"w":"word","start":147.066},{"w":"ending","start":147.346},{"w":"in","start":147.636},{"w":"\"l","start":147.926},{"w":"y\"","start":148.216},{"w":"is","start":148.506},{"w":"often","start":148.786},{"w":"an","start":149.186},{"w":"adverb,","start":149.346},{"w":"like","start":149.77},{"w":"\"quickly\".","start":150.195}]},{"id":"c34","start":151.019,"end":156.195,"marks":{},"text":"And a word ending in \"e d\" or \"i n g\" is often a verb, like \"walked\" or \"walking\".","words":[{"w":"And","start":151.019},{"w":"a","start":151.139},{"w":"word","start":151.259},{"w":"ending","start":151.539},{"w":"in","start":151.899},{"w":"\"e","start":152.099},{"w":"d\"","start":152.339},{"w":"or","start":152.579},{"w":"\"i","start":152.899},{"w":"n","start":153.139},{"w":"g\"","start":153.379},{"w":"is","start":153.579},{"w":"often","start":153.819},{"w":"a","start":154.099},{"w":"verb,","start":154.379},{"w":"like","start":154.659},{"w":"\"walked\"","start":154.939},{"w":"or","start":155.379},{"w":"\"walking\".","start":155.659}]}],"title":"Clues a tagger uses","shortTitle":"Clues a tagger uses","props":{"kicker":"Clues","title":"Clues a tagger looks for","items":[{"text":"After “the” or “a”, usually a noun"},{"text":"After “to”, often a verb"},{"text":"Ends in -ly: often an adverb"},{"text":"Ends in -ed or -ing: often a verb"}],"numbered":false},"start":136.433,"end":156.195,"startFrame":4093,"durationInFrames":620},{"id":"accuracy","kind":"core","component":"BarChart","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c35","start":157.1,"end":160.583,"marks":{},"text":"How good are taggers? On English news text, they are very good.","words":[{"w":"How","start":157.1},{"w":"good","start":157.34},{"w":"are","start":157.54},{"w":"taggers?","start":157.94},{"w":"On","start":158.34},{"w":"English","start":158.58},{"w":"news","start":158.98},{"w":"text,","start":159.26},{"w":"they","start":159.66},{"w":"are","start":159.78},{"w":"very","start":159.98},{"w":"good.","start":160.26}]},{"id":"c36","start":160.983,"end":166.545,"marks":{},"text":"Just picking each word's most common tag already gets about ninety-two percent of words right.","words":[{"w":"Just","start":160.983},{"w":"picking","start":161.263},{"w":"each","start":161.623},{"w":"word's","start":161.943},{"w":"most","start":162.303},{"w":"common","start":162.583},{"w":"tag","start":162.943},{"w":"already","start":163.423},{"w":"gets","start":163.983},{"w":"about","start":164.263},{"w":"ninety-two","start":164.73},{"w":"percent","start":165.196},{"w":"of","start":165.663},{"w":"words","start":165.863},{"w":"right.","start":166.223}]},{"id":"c37","start":166.945,"end":179.072,"marks":{},"text":"Modern taggers, which use the whole sentence, reach about ninety-seven percent. That still means roughly one word in thirty gets the wrong tag, and the hard cases are exactly the ambiguous ones.","words":[{"w":"Modern","start":166.945},{"w":"taggers,","start":167.465},{"w":"which","start":168.065},{"w":"use","start":168.305},{"w":"the","start":168.545},{"w":"whole","start":168.705},{"w":"sentence,","start":169.025},{"w":"reach","start":169.745},{"w":"about","start":170.145},{"w":"ninety-seven","start":170.785},{"w":"percent.","start":171.425},{"w":"That","start":172.065},{"w":"still","start":172.385},{"w":"means","start":172.745},{"w":"roughly","start":173.145},{"w":"one","start":173.585},{"w":"word","start":173.825},{"w":"in","start":174.065},{"w":"thirty","start":174.265},{"w":"gets","start":174.665},{"w":"the","start":174.945},{"w":"wrong","start":175.145},{"w":"tag,","start":175.465},{"w":"and","start":175.945},{"w":"the","start":176.145},{"w":"hard","start":176.345},{"w":"cases","start":176.625},{"w":"are","start":177.105},{"w":"exactly","start":177.305},{"w":"the","start":177.865},{"w":"ambiguous","start":177.985},{"w":"ones.","start":178.705}]}],"title":"How good are taggers?","shortTitle":"How good are taggers?","props":{"kicker":"How good is it?","title":"Tagging accuracy on English news text","unit":"%","bars":[{"label":"Most common tag","value":92},{"label":"Modern tagger","value":97}],"note":"About 1 word in 30 still gets the wrong tag."},"start":157.1,"end":179.072,"startFrame":4713,"durationInFrames":687},{"id":"quiz","kind":"quiz","component":"Quiz","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c38","start":180,"end":186.021,"marks":{},"text":"Time for a quick quiz. In the sentence \"Time flies like an arrow\", what part of speech is \"flies\"?","words":[{"w":"Time","start":180},{"w":"for","start":180.32},{"w":"a","start":180.62},{"w":"quick","start":180.92},{"w":"quiz.","start":181.22},{"w":"In","start":181.52},{"w":"the","start":181.72},{"w":"sentence","start":181.92},{"w":"\"Time","start":182.72},{"w":"flies","start":183},{"w":"like","start":183.52},{"w":"an","start":183.68},{"w":"arrow\",","start":183.84},{"w":"what","start":184.24},{"w":"part","start":184.44},{"w":"of","start":184.64},{"w":"speech","start":184.76},{"w":"is","start":185.16},{"w":"\"flies\"?","start":185.36}]},{"id":"c39","start":186.421,"end":189.927,"marks":{},"text":"Pause the video and choose: noun, verb, or adjective?","words":[{"w":"Pause","start":186.421},{"w":"the","start":186.701},{"w":"video","start":186.941},{"w":"and","start":187.181},{"w":"choose:","start":187.381},{"w":"noun,","start":187.914},{"w":"verb,","start":188.448},{"w":"or","start":188.981},{"w":"adjective?","start":189.141}]},{"id":"c40","start":193.327,"end":201.239,"marks":{},"text":"It's a verb: flying is what time does. But in \"Fruit flies like a banana\", \"flies\" is a noun. Same word, different neighbours.","words":[{"w":"It's","start":193.327},{"w":"a","start":193.567},{"w":"verb:","start":193.807},{"w":"flying","start":194.047},{"w":"is","start":194.487},{"w":"what","start":194.687},{"w":"time","start":194.927},{"w":"does.","start":195.247},{"w":"But","start":195.687},{"w":"in","start":195.927},{"w":"\"Fruit","start":196.127},{"w":"flies","start":196.487},{"w":"like","start":196.887},{"w":"a","start":197.047},{"w":"banana\",","start":197.167},{"w":"\"flies\"","start":197.887},{"w":"is","start":198.607},{"w":"a","start":198.767},{"w":"noun.","start":198.927},{"w":"Same","start":199.447},{"w":"word,","start":199.887},{"w":"different","start":200.207},{"w":"neighbours.","start":200.647}]}],"title":"Quick quiz","shortTitle":"Quick quiz: “Time flies like an arrow”","props":{"kicker":"Pause and predict","question":"In “Time flies like an arrow”, what part of speech is “flies”?","options":["Noun","Verb","Adjective"],"answer":1,"explain":"It's the action time does. In “Fruit flies like a banana”, it's a noun!"},"start":180,"end":201.239,"startFrame":5400,"durationInFrames":665},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","component":"Recap","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c41","start":202.167,"end":206.411,"marks":{},"text":"Let's recap. A part of speech is the role a word plays in a sentence.","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":202.167},{"w":"recap.","start":202.567},{"w":"A","start":203.167},{"w":"part","start":203.407},{"w":"of","start":203.607},{"w":"speech","start":203.767},{"w":"is","start":204.247},{"w":"the","start":204.367},{"w":"role","start":204.527},{"w":"a","start":204.807},{"w":"word","start":204.967},{"w":"plays","start":205.247},{"w":"in","start":205.567},{"w":"a","start":205.687},{"w":"sentence.","start":205.847}]},{"id":"c42","start":206.811,"end":211.062,"marks":{},"text":"A tagger labels every word with a tag, like NOUN, VERB or DET.","words":[{"w":"A","start":206.811},{"w":"tagger","start":207.071},{"w":"labels","start":207.331},{"w":"every","start":207.771},{"w":"word","start":208.051},{"w":"with","start":208.291},{"w":"a","start":208.411},{"w":"tag,","start":208.571},{"w":"like","start":209.091},{"w":"NOUN,","start":209.544},{"w":"VERB","start":209.998},{"w":"or","start":210.451},{"w":"DET.","start":210.757}]},{"id":"c43","start":211.462,"end":214.296,"marks":{},"text":"Many words, like \"book\", can take more than one tag.","words":[{"w":"Many","start":211.462},{"w":"words,","start":211.782},{"w":"like","start":212.102},{"w":"\"book\",","start":212.382},{"w":"can","start":212.742},{"w":"take","start":212.982},{"w":"more","start":213.222},{"w":"than","start":213.422},{"w":"one","start":213.622},{"w":"tag.","start":213.862}]},{"id":"c44","start":214.696,"end":217.302,"marks":{},"text":"And the neighbouring words decide which tag fits.","words":[{"w":"And","start":214.696},{"w":"the","start":214.776},{"w":"neighbouring","start":214.856},{"w":"words","start":215.456},{"w":"decide","start":215.776},{"w":"which","start":216.256},{"w":"tag","start":216.456},{"w":"fits.","start":216.816}]},{"id":"c45","start":217.702,"end":222.621,"marks":{},"text":"Next lesson: Word Vectors. How can a computer know that 'rain' is close to 'storm'?","words":[{"w":"Next","start":218.118},{"w":"lesson:","start":218.534},{"w":"Word","start":218.95},{"w":"Vectors.","start":219.366},{"w":"How","start":219.782},{"w":"can","start":220.022},{"w":"a","start":220.222},{"w":"computer","start":220.342},{"w":"know","start":220.822},{"w":"that","start":220.982},{"w":"'rain'","start":221.182},{"w":"is","start":221.502},{"w":"close","start":221.662},{"w":"to","start":221.942},{"w":"'storm'?","start":222.142}]}],"title":"Recap and next lesson","shortTitle":"Recap and next lesson","props":{"title":"Recap","points":["A part of speech is the role a word plays","Taggers label every word: NOUN, VERB, DET…","Many words can take more than one tag","The neighbouring words decide which tag fits"],"next":{"title":"Word Vectors","question":"How can a computer know that 'rain' is close to 'storm'?"}},"start":202.167,"end":222.621,"startFrame":6065,"durationInFrames":659}],"refs":{"c01":0.6,"c02":7.335,"c03":13.667,"c04":23.1,"c05":30.196,"c06":34.134,"c07":43.567,"c08":48.911,"c09":52.488,"c10":57.192,"c11":61.32,"c12":65.332,"c13":69.334,"c14":74.867,"c15":78.242,"c16":79.812,"c17":81.355,"c18":86.317,"c19":89.099,"c20":90.786,"c21":93.067,"c22":96.675,"c23":100.012,"c24":103.778,"c25":108.261,"c25@verdict":110.381,"c26":113.033,"c27":117.054,"c28":